Rebased and pushed three changes:

* The UPGRADE note told users to pass the transport names explicitly to keep in-process handling. That gives asynchronous sending instead, so it did not produce the behaviour it promised. It now points to an empty `TransportNamesStamp` on the inner envelope, which does work, and mentions that the handler returns `null` once the message is sent.
* The handler tested `$message->transportNames` for truthiness, so a transport literally named `0` was ignored when passed as a string while `['0']` still worked. Empty strings are filtered now, so both forms behave the same.
* The tests go through a real `MessageBus` and `SendersLocator` instead of asserting on the stamps passed to a bus mock, so they observe which sender receives the message.

